[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106020,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma (EHE) is a malignant vascular neoplasm composed of epithelioid endothelial cells in a myxohyaline stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106021,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9133/3 Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>9133/3 Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma with <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>CAMTA1</em> fusion</p>\r\n<p>9133/3 Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma with <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em> fusion</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106022,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B5Y &amp; XH9GF8 Other specified malignant mesenchymal neoplasms &amp; Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106023,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> malignant epithelioid haemangioendothelioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106024,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma with <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>CAMTA1</em> fusion; epithelioid haemangioendothelioma with <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em> fusion</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106025,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Almost any organ can be affected. Most cases arise in somatic soft tissues, bone, lung, and liver {31724797; 20333551; 31814291}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106026,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Presentation varies depending on location. Patients with soft tissue EHE usually present with a painful mass. A high incidence of multiorgan disease is reported in children {31724797}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106027,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EHE is very rare in children. It occurs at a median age of 13.8&nbsp;years in this population and has no sex predilection {31724797}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106028,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106029,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "<p>EHE is characterized by a t(1;3)(p36;q25) translocation resulting in a <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>CAMTA1</em> fusion {21885404; 21584898}. The resulting WWTR1&nbsp;(TAZ)::CAMTA1 chimeric protein disrupts the Hippo pathway, and the protein is located in the nucleus, with constitutive activation {25961935}. An alternative fusion, <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em>, is detected in rare cases {23737213}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-10T15:49:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106030,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cut surface is typically white and firm. Origin from a vessel may be seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106031,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EHE is an infiltrative tumour composed of cords and nests of bland epithelioid tumour cells with round nuclei, eosinophilic cytoplasm, and variable intracytoplasmic vacuoles in a myxohyaline stroma. Angiocentric growth, which can be occlusive, is seen in some cases {7093931; 9130982; 24986479}. A small subset of tumours have nuclear atypia and more mitotic activity. By immunohistochemistry, they are typically positive for ERG, CD31, and CAMTA1, and they are variably positive for keratins, SMA, CD34, and podoplanin {26414223; 31662570}. Immunoreactivity for cytokeratin is seen in a minority {9130982}. Nuclear expression of TFE3 is seen in most cases, irrespective of <em>TFE3</em> rearrangement {24986479}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106032,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106033,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Identification of the <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>CAMTA1</em> or <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em> fusions {21885404; 21584898}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106034,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> cords and nests of epithelioid cells in a myxohyaline stroma; immunoreactivity for endothelial markers, CAMTA1, or TFE3.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> molecular confirmation of <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>CAMTA1</em> or <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em>.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106035,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>For somatic tumours, the eighth-edition Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) or American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) staging system is used. AJCC staging is not applicable for abdominal or thoracic tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106036,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 414,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EHE is unpredictable; some cases have an indolent course and others are aggressive. Metastasis is seen in as many as 21% of cases and mortality in as many as 17% {18551749; 9130982}. In adults, stratification into high-risk and low-risk groups based on a combination of mitotic activity and tumour size has shown a worse prognosis for patients with both high mitotic activity (&gt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup>, equating to &gt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;mitoses/50&nbsp;HPF of 0.5&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> in area) and large tumour size (&gt; 30 mm) than for patients with neither feature (respective 5-year disease-specific survival rates: 59% vs 100%) {18551749}. Atypical histological features are not predictive {18551749}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:49:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]